  "name": "Tanzania",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "verification": "draft",
  "notes": [
    "The NIDA number format (20 digits) is from a secondary validator page read from the search index; NIDA publishes no format a fetched page states. Every other identifier is free text.",
    "The 31 regions are the ISO 3166-2:TZ list read from a secondary copy of the ISO table (Wikipedia, fetched); no official Tanzanian code list was found. No district or ward list is bundled: both are free text.",
    "The Public Holidays Act (Cap. 35) text was read from the search index only (the OAG revised edition and the TanzLII copy are PDFs that would not fetch; the tanzanialaws.com copy returned 404). Karume Day and Saba Saba are not in the Schedule as read and are kept as draft, as presidential declarations listed by the Bank of Tanzania for 2025.",
    "Nyerere Day (14 October) is in the revised Schedule read from the search index (R.E. 2023, with GN 486 of 2022); the date it began is not confirmed.",
    "Id-ul-Fitr, Id-el-Haj and Maulidi depend on the moon: the Act gives two days for Id-ul-Fitr, but the only dates found are the Bank of Tanzania's list for 2025, one date each, read from the search index. No other year is listed.",
    "The Act moves a holiday that falls on a Saturday or a Sunday to the next day that is not itself a holiday (section 4). The pack's observed rule covers only the Sunday; a Saturday holiday is kept on its own day here.",
    "The PAYE and SDL due day (the 7th of the month after) is stated by the Tanzania Revenue Authority; the TRA pages would not fetch, so both are draft. NSSF, PSSSF and WCF are due 'within one month after month end', which the due rules cannot state, so they are not modelled."
  ],
